+Creating STRICT tables
+======================
+
+SQLite 3.37 and higher supports `STRICT tables
+<https://www.sqlite.org/stricttables.html>`__, which reject values that do not
+match the declared column type. Pass ``strict=True`` when creating a table::
+
+    db["authors"].create(
+        {"id": int, "name": str, "score": float},
+        pk="id",
+        strict=True,
+    )
+
+You can also pass ``strict=True`` to ``insert()``, ``insert_all()``,
+``upsert()``, ``upsert_all()`` or ``lookup()`` when those methods create a new table.
+The ``table.strict`` property reports whether an existing table is strict.
+
